<section class="band-navy" id="how" aria-labelledby="how-title">
  <div class="wrap section">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">How it works</p>
      <h2 id="how-title">How each figure is sourced and checked</h2>
    </div>
    <ol class="flow" style="--n:5">
      <li><h3>Pin the sources</h3><p>The OAIC's July to December 2025 workbook is pinned by its hash, and the 18 OAIC reports from 2018 to 2024 are transcribed into a registry.</p></li>
      <li><h3>Label every figure</h3><p>Each figure is marked as a published period figure, a published month figure, or a platform sum of published figures.</p></li>
      <li><h3>Keep restatements visible</h3><p>When a later report restates a figure, the latest value is shown, the first-published value is kept beside it, and the restating report is named.</p></li>
      <li><h3>Check at start-up</h3><p>The platform re-sums its facts against hand-verified published totals for every period from 2018 to 2025. A mismatch stops the service.</p></li>
      <li><h3>Serve with lineage</h3><p>Every figure links to where it came from, and the same figures are available through a read-only API.</p></li>
    </ol>
    <div class="boundary">
      <div>
        <h3>What the AI does</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Turns a plain-language description into a dashboard layout with citations.</li>
          <li>Answers questions grounded in the data notes and the published figures.</li>
          <li>Drafts the structure of reports built from the same figures.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="never">
        <h3>What it is built not to do</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Write a number:</strong> the platform computes every figure.</li>
          <li><strong>Give legal advice:</strong> or say whether a specific incident is an eligible data breach.</li>
          <li><strong>Identify anyone:</strong> the chat refuses requests that would identify a breach, an entity or an individual.</li>
          <li><strong>Fill a gap:</strong> an unpublished period stays a disclosed gap.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="boundary-note">As stated in the demo's reference pages.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band-mist" id="inside" aria-labelledby="inside-title">
  <div class="wrap section" data-acc-scope>
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Inside the product</p>
      <h2 id="inside-title">Every view, and what it shows</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="acc-head">
      <h3>Views</h3>
      <button type="button" class="btn-text" data-expand-all hidden><span class="js-label">Expand all</span><span class="visually-hidden"> views</span></button>
    </div>
    <div class="points">
      <details id="ndb-overview"><summary><span class="acc-title">NDB at a glance</span><span class="hint">The latest period on one page</span></summary><div class="acc-body">
        <p>Notifications for the latest half-year and the change on the same half last year, the main sources of breach, the share identified within 10 days and notified within 30 days, a "What the data says" summary and the historical trend.</p>
      </div></details>
      <details id="ndb-notifications"><summary><span class="acc-title">Notifications</span><span class="hint">By month, and the series since 2018</span></summary><div class="acc-body">
        <ul>
          <li>Notifications by month from the latest workbook.</li>
          <li>The historical series from 2018, including a restatement table that shows first-published and latest values.</li>
        </ul>
      </div></details>
      <details id="ndb-breach-detail"><summary><span class="acc-title">Breach detail</span><span class="hint">Who and what was affected, and how</span></summary><div class="acc-body">
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Individuals affected:</strong> published in ranges. The large-breach threshold changed over the series, so it travels with each figure.</li>
          <li><strong>Kinds of information:</strong> contact, identity, financial, health, tax file numbers, other sensitive information and, from 2025, digital ID.</li>
          <li><strong>Source of breach:</strong> malicious or criminal attack, human error and system fault.</li>
          <li><strong>Top sectors</strong>, and <strong>sectors and movers</strong>.</li>
        </ul>
      </div></details>
      <details id="ndb-time"><summary><span class="acc-title">Time</span><span class="hint">To identify, respond and notify</span></summary><div class="acc-body">
        <p>Time taken in calendar days from when the entity became aware of the incident, from the workbook's bands. The 30-day window reflects the assessment obligation in section 26WH of the Privacy Act. Where no whole-period median is published, no median is shown.</p>
      </div></details>
      <details id="ndb-reference"><summary><span class="acc-title">Reference</span><span class="hint">The definitional authority for every figure</span></summary><div class="acc-body">
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Data notes:</strong> what the figures count, the categories, publication cadence and known source quirks. The chat answers are grounded in this text.</li>
          <li><strong>How to use</strong>, <strong>API access</strong> and <strong>data provenance</strong>.</li>
        </ul>
      </div></details>
      <details id="ndb-api"><summary><span class="acc-title">API</span><span class="hint">The same figures, as read-only JSON</span></summary><div class="acc-body">
        <ul>
          <li><code>/api/</code>: dataset information, dimensions and keys.</li>
          <li><code>/api/figures</code>: every platform-computed figure with its basis.</li>
          <li><code>/api/facts</code>: the underlying facts, filterable by period, month, dimension, category and measure.</li>
          <li><code>/api/measures</code>: the dimensions and their measures.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>The API never returns a number the platform did not compute from the pinned sources.</p>
      </div></details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

